Backlog fix L1 — recirc "Already running" x4 log noise
=======================================================
Automation id: 1789000001001  ("Рециркуляция ГВС по расписанию + присутствие")

Problem: mode: single + three overlapping triggers (time_pattern /10, presence
state, night_saver state) can re-fire while a prior run is still in-flight for an
instant. HA then logs a WARNING "... Already running" (seen x4 at 03:55). The run
that is dropped changes nothing - the choose block is idempotent (only toggles the
switch when it is in the wrong state), so no behavior is lost.

Fix: add `max_exceeded: silent`. This keeps mode: single (extra concurrent triggers
are still dropped exactly as before - zero runtime-behavior change) and only
suppresses the WARNING log line. `mode: restart`/`mode: queued` were rejected
because they WOULD change which runs execute.

Deploy: RELOAD-only - POST /api/services/automation/reload (no HA restart needed).
Apply from the directory containing automations.yaml with:
    patch -p1 < backlog_recirc.patch      (or: git apply -p1 backlog_recirc.patch)
Diff is against automations.yaml as fetched from /config on 2026-07-16.

--- a/automations.yaml
+++ b/automations.yaml
@@ -4148,6 +4148,7 @@
     выключен: экономия ~15-20 кВт·ч/мес + бак ГВС меньше остывает (бойлер реже
     догревает). Ночную экономию не трогает — рециркуляция убрана из 1784000001002.
   mode: single
+  max_exceeded: silent
   triggers:
   - trigger: time_pattern
     minutes: /10
